{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:1ffdfde8b72eab8f","name":"MR-200-Series Minesweeper Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-1ffdfde8b72eab8f","title":"MR-200-Series Minesweeper Droid","revision":20909,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T00:46:29Z","sha256":"ace12108ad34ac331e7182a60133674a771db402e8220ebd4cb1998213b8afed","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20909","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=MR-200-Series%20Minesweeper%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-1ffdfde8b72eab8f","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Galaxy at War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Galaxy_at_War"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Confederacy of Independent Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Confederacy_of_Independent_Systems","referenceId":"reference:dfc46c9d666b9b41"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Baktoid MR-200-Series Minesweeper Droid is first deployed early in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Clone Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Clone_Wars"}," by Separatist forces. With both sides engaged in prolonged trench warfare, the battlefields on some planets became static, and minefields are used to dissuade attack or protect strategic locations. The MR-200 effectively clears the worst of these areas, cutting a path through a heavily mined zone so that Battle Droids can pass safely. In a pinch, the Minesweeper Droid also make an excellent Shocktrooper Droid, flushing out tunnels or trenches that shelter enemy troops. The Droid is notoriously single-minded, and when lacking other orders, it rolls back and forth over the same ground, hoping to detonate any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mines"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mines"}," it may have missed. The MR-200 flags ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mines"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mines"}," that do not detonate or that otherwise survive its brute-force tactics. This information is relayed back to the Central Control Computer, so that all allied ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," do not mistakenly enter the minefield.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Minesweeper Droid is a curiously shaped mix of high and low tech. The main body uses repulsorlift technology to safely float over the ground that it is clearing. However, the front of the Droid is composed of a large, metallic drum covered in lengths of durable chain. As the Droid floats along, the drum rotates, flailing the chains and beating the ground to detonate any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mines"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mines"}," it contacts. Although tough, the drum becomes battered and mangled from repeated explosions, so it is designed for easy replacement between missions. The Droid's repulsorlift is powerful enough to lift the drum off the ground, so the Minesweeper Droid is able to ignore ",{"tag":"a","children":["Difficult Terrain"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Difficult_Terrain"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["MR-200-Series Minesweeper Droids can't be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["MR-200-Series Minesweeper Droid Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Large ",{"tag":"a","children":["5th-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/5th-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 3\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," "